          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            243,
            246
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " This type is a sort of \"double cursor\". It tracks three regions in the buffer: a region at the beginning of the",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            247,
            362
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " buffer that has been logically filled with data, a region that has been initialized at some point but not yet",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            363,
            476
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " logically filled, and a region at the end that is fully uninitialized. The filled region is guaranteed to be a",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            477,
            591
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " subset of the initialized region.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            592,
            629
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            630,
            633
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " In summary, the contents of the buffer can be visualized as:",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            634,
            698
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " ```not_rust",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            699,
            714
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [             capacity              ]",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            715,
            756
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [ filled |         unfilled         ]",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            757,
            798
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [    initialized    | uninitialized ]",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            799,
            840
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " ```",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            841,
            848
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            849,
            852
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " A `BorrowedBuf` is created around some existing data (or capacity for data) via a unique reference",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            853,
            955
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " (`&mut`). The `BorrowedBuf` can be configured (e.g., using `clear` or `set_init`), but cannot be",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            956,
            1056
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " directly written. To write into the buffer, use `unfilled` to create a `BorrowedCursor`. The cursor",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1057,
            1160
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " has write-only access to the unfilled portion of the buffer (you can think of it as a",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1161,
            1250
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " write-only iterator).",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1251,
            1276
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1277,
            1280
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " The lifetime `'data` is a bound on the lifetime of the underlying data.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1281,
            1356
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        }
      ],
